            </summary>
            <returns></returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:ClearCanvas.Common.Actions.XmlActionCompiler`1">
            <summary>
            Compiler for compiling a set of actions to execute from an XML file.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            The <see cref="T:ClearCanvas.Common.Actions.XmlActionCompiler`1"/> can be used to compile a set of actions to perform
            from XML.  The <see cref="M:ClearCanvas.Common.Actions.XmlActionCompiler`1.Compile(System.Xml.XmlElement,System.Boolean)"/> method can be called to create the
            set of actions to be performed.  These actions can then be executed based on input data.
            </para>
            <para>
            Action operators are defined by an extension point supplied to the constructor, or can be manually supplied.
            The compiler does not contain any predefined operators.  The compiler makes no assumptions
            about the attributes of the <see cref="T:System.Xml.XmlElement"/> for the operator.  Any attributes can be defined
            for the operator and are interpreted by the operation defined for the action type.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:ClearCanvas.Common.Actions.XmlActionCompiler`1.#ctor(ClearCanvas.Common.IExtensionPoint)">
            <summary>
            Constructor.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:ClearCanvas.Common.Actions.XmlActionCompiler`1.#ctor(System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable{ClearCanvas.Common.Actions.IXmlActionCompilerOperator{`0}})">
            <summary>
            Constructor.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="P:ClearCanvas.Common.Actions.XmlActionCompiler`1.Schema">
            <summary>
            A compiled XML schema used by the compiler to verify specifications.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:ClearCanvas.Common.Actions.XmlActionCompiler`1.Compile(System.Xml.XmlElement,System.Boolean)">
            <summary>
            Compile a set of actions to perform.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            This method will parse the child <see cref="T:System.Xml.XmlElement"/>s of <paramref name="containingNode"/>.
            Based on the name of the element, the the compiler will look for an action that handles the element type.
            A list is constructed of all actions to perform, and a class implementing the 
            <see cref="T:ClearCanvas.Common.Actions.IActionList`1"/> interface is returned which can be called to exectute the actions based on input data.
            </para>
            </remarks>
            <param name="containingNode">The input XML containg actions to perform.</param>
            <param name="checkSchema">Check the schema when compiling.</param>
            <returns>A class instance that implements the <see cref="T:ClearCanvas.Common.Actions.IActionList`1"/> interface.</returns>
        </member>
        <member name="T:ClearCanvas.Common.Actions.XmlActionCompilerException">
            <summary>
            Exception thrown by <see cref="T:ClearCanvas.Common.Actions.XmlActionCompiler`1"/> or extension operators.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="M:ClearCanvas.Common.Actions.XmlActionCompilerException.#ctor(System.String)">
            <summary>
            Constructor.
            </summary>
            <param name="message">Descriptive message associated with the exception.</param>
        </member>
        <member name="M:ClearCanvas.Common.Actions.XmlActionCompilerException.#ctor(System.String,System.Exception)">
            <summary>
            Constructor.
            </summary>
            <param name="message">Descriptive message associated with the exception.</param>
            <param name="innerException">The inner exception.</param>
        </member>
