        </member>
        <member name="T:ClearCanvas.Common.GuiToolkitAttribute">
            <summary>
            Attribute used to mark a class as using a specific GUI toolkit.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Typically this attribute is used on an extension class (in addition to the <see cref="T:ClearCanvas.Common.ExtensionOfAttribute"/>) 
            to allow plugin code to determine at runtime if the given extension is compatible with the GUI toolkit
            that is currently in use by the main window.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="M:ClearCanvas.Common.GuiToolkitAttribute.#ctor(System.String)">
            <summary>
