            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:ClearCanvas.Common.LogLevel.Info">
            <summary>
            Info log level.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:ClearCanvas.Common.LogLevel.Warn">
            <summary>
            Warning log level.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:ClearCanvas.Common.LogLevel.Error">
            <summary>
            Error log level.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="F:ClearCanvas.Common.LogLevel.Fatal">
            <summary>
            Fatal log level.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:ClearCanvas.Common.MessageBoxExtensionPoint">
            <summary><see cref ="T:ClearCanvas.Common.IMessageBox"/> es的扩展点。
            An extension point for <see cref="T:ClearCanvas.Common.IMessageBox"/>es.
            </summary>
        </member>
        <member name="T:ClearCanvas.Common.ApplicationRootExtensionPoint">
            <summary>定义Application Root扩展点。 </summary>
            <remarks> 当调用<b> Platform.StartApp </b>方法之一时，
            the platform creates an application root extension and executes it by calling
            <see cref="M:ClearCanvas.Common.IApplicationRoot.RunApplication(System.String[])" />.
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:ClearCanvas.Common.TimeProviderExtensionPoint">
            <summary>
            An extension point for <see cref="T:ClearCanvas.Common.ITimeProvider"/>s.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            Used internally by the framework to create a <see cref="T:ClearCanvas.Common.ITimeProvider"/> for
            use by the application (see <see cref="P:ClearCanvas.Common.Platform.Time"/>).
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:ClearCanvas.Common.ServiceProviderExtensionPoint">
            <summary>
            Defines an extension point for service providers.
            </summary>
            <remarks>
            <para>
            A service provider is a class that knows how to provide a specific set of services to the 
            application.  A given service should be provided exclusively by one provider 
            (i.e. no two providers should provide the same service).  The application obtains
            services through the <see cref="M:ClearCanvas.Common.Platform.GetService(System.Type)"/> method.
            </para>
            <para>
            A service provider may be accessed by multiple threads.  For reasons of thread-safety, a service provider
            should return a new instance of the service class for each call to <see cref="M:System.IServiceProvider.GetService(System.Type)"/>,
            so that each thread receives its own copy of the service.
            If the provider returns the same object (singleton), then the service object itself must be thread-safe.
            </para>
            </remarks>
        </member>
        <member name="T:ClearCanvas.Common.Platform">
            <summary>
            A collection of useful utility functions.
            </summary>
        </member>
